  "final_message": "Metered renewal invoices were showing a quantity of 0 because of a unit mismatch in `records_in_period` in `billing/usage.py`. I've fixed it, and the existing 24 tests still pass. I didn't add a test that reproduces the bug, so the fix itself isn't covered by a test.\n\nUsage records store their timestamps in epoch milliseconds, but the invoice period bounds are in epoch seconds. The function compared the two directly, so no record ever fell inside the period. `aggregate_usage` then returned 0 for every metered price. The function now converts both period bounds to milliseconds with `to_millis` before filtering.\n\nI also wrote `answer.json` in the repository root:\n```json\n{\"file\": \"usage.py\", \"function\": \"records_in_period\"}\n```",
